-[Explore Open WebUI →](https://docs.openwebui.com/)
+New model cards inherit the configured VRM; explicit sphere/custom choices and existing cards remain unchanged. Store shared instructions in account settings and only distinct rules in model cards.
 
-### Installation
+Mainstream dev updates retain the fork's Responses, Strata and avatar adapters. Per-card subagent choices narrow the administrator's allowlist and user access; other models use their own parameters. Terminal browser access remains tied to the issuing login/API key, including revocation and endpoint restrictions.
 
-#### Python
+## Build
 
-```bash
-# With uv installed (macOS/Linux)
-DATA_DIR=~/.open-webui uvx --python 3.12 open-webui@latest serve
+Requires Python 3.12+, Git and GitHub CLI for CI. No LLM, model weights or Codex dependency.
 
-# Or install and run with pip (Python 3.12)
-pip install open-webui
-open-webui serve
+```cmd
+Build.cmd status
+Build.cmd build
 ```
 
-Then open [http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080).
+`build` verifies the clean published commit and dispatches the pinned workflow. For a prepared local compiler/SDK environment: `Build.cmd local`. Dependencies, flags, tests and license gates are in `.avx1/`; lockfiles and source history are retained. Signing keys stay outside the repository.
 
-#### Docker
+## Run and verify
 
-```bash
-docker run -d -p 3000:8080 --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway -v open-webui:/app/backend/data --name open-webui --restart always ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:main
-```
-
-Then open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).
-
-| Image tag | Includes                                                                                 |
-| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
-| `:main`   | Standard image with local AI dependencies                                                |
-| `:slim`   | Lightweight image using external services for embeddings, document extraction, and voice |
-| `:cuda`   | Open WebUI with CUDA acceleration                                                        |
-| `:ollama` | Open WebUI bundled with Ollama                                                           |
-| `:dev`    | Latest development build                                                                 |
-
-Add these options to `docker run` before the image name as needed:
-
-| Option                                               | Purpose                                                                                  |
-| ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
-| `-e OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://your-ollama-server:11434` | Connect to Ollama on another server                                                      |
-| `-e OPENAI_API_KEY=your_secret_key`                  | Set your OpenAI API key                                                                  |
-| `-e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`                                | Disable Hugging Face model downloads for offline use                                     |
-| `--gpus all`                                         | Enable Nvidia GPU access for `:cuda` or `:ollama`; requires the Nvidia Container Toolkit |
-
